Focus claims:
- OldRenderPos only set at spawn / UpdateRenderSectorList never skips: CONFIRMED.
  `grep -rni oldrenderpos` over the whole tree: p_secnodes.cpp:378, :382 (reads), p_mobj.cpp:5437 (spawn write = FLT_MAX), actor.h:1188 (decl).
  No serializer entry, no DEFINE_FIELD. The guard `Pos() != OldRenderPos` is therefore always true.
  Body re-read line by line (p_secnodes.cpp:375-427): ClearRenderLineList + optional linePortals scan + ClearRenderSectorList + up/down sector-portal walks. Portal-free map cost (2x P_DelSeclist(nullptr), 2x PortalBlocksMovement) confirmed.
  CORRECTED the proposed fix (see #9).
- FState::CallAction per-call heap copies: CONFIRMED.
  info.cpp:172 CheckCallerType called every call; info.cpp:135 `auto argtypes = ActionFunc->Proto->ArgumentTypes;` (by value, TArray<PType*> types.h:704);
  TArray copy ctor tarray.h:247-250 -> DoCopy tarray.h:848-858 M_Malloc when Count != 0 (always: includes self).
  info.cpp:179 `auto defs = ActionFunc->DefaultArgs;` (TArray<TypedVMValue>, vm.h:440) second copy when DefaultArgs nonempty;
  DefaultArgs filled only when the declaration has defaults (zcc_compile.cpp:2874-2877). A_Chase (actor.zs:1287, 3 optional params) and direct-function mapping (codegen.cpp:9798-9811 GetDirectFunction, vmbuilder.cpp:802-814) confirmed -> 2 mallocs per A_Chase; A_Look -> 1.
- "GC runs twice per frame": PARTLY CORRECT, reworded.
  GC::CheckGC() is called exactly twice per main-loop iteration: d_net.cpp:2192 (first stmt of TryRunTics) and d_main.cpp:1115 (D_Display, before the nodrawers return). `grep -rn CheckGC src` finds no other callers. Main loop d_main.cpp:1463-1467.
  But CheckGC only calls Step() when State > GCS_Pause or AllocBytes >= Threshold (dobjgc.cpp:155-163), and Step's budget = max(GCMINSTEPSIZE, avg-bytes-per-CheckGC-call * StepMul/100) with a 512-call history (dobjgc.cpp:80-93, 331-335, 704-727). So more calls means proportionally smaller steps; total GC work follows the allocation rate, not the call count.

